oc=AdmtOxv9c_cbRX3TfRmzP8blQ6_728vVmoDv6PvFK1AgphlHtHRTpoYAEXfcVqXQDEw&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-3.oculuscdn.com&oh=00_AfuPr8tGElr2K2ty1o_G4NaKpbA_NnusPDUoi1N8broAsg&oe=69A44055"}, {"file_name": "2 Screenshot 2560x1440.png", "id": "1219888766768995", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-3.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/499617762_1219888770102328_625861554141402806_n.png?_nc_cat=110&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=EMlB-io03vkQ7kNvwEA26aF&_nc_oc=AdklalDGfLr0js2b7uiUYBG1iYWcbq6qgEWnNS-wYA4GgiwQwtPvZXvGOqDxl6m7ffA&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-3.oculuscdn.com&oh=00_AfuphvwGULSxaNgLVAsps5D5YDKlFU6MCkUVCVD7zd6kDA&oe=69A437EF"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "IMVR", "keywords": ["imvr", "interactionwithnature", "longlamai", "Penan", "molong"], "long_description": "IMVR is a co-designed virtual reality experience developed in close collaboration with the Penan community of Long Lamai, Sarawak (East Malaysia).\n\nRooted in the indigenous concept of Molong, a philosophy of care, custodianship, and reciprocal relationships with nature, IMVR invites users to experience the rainforest not as an observer, but as a part of it. \n\n**What you can experience**\n\n- Explore a 3D rainforest environment inspired by the Borneo rainforest\n- Choose a living entity (Olong) and see the world from its perspective\n- Immerse yourself in authentic forest soundscapes\n- Learn about indigenous ecological values through embodied interaction\n\n**Why IMVR** \n\nIMVR fosters ecological awareness, and a deeper emotional connection with the forest (tana), through immersion, not instruction.", "short_description": "IMVR is a co-designed virtual reality experience developed with the Penan community of Long Lamai in Sarawak, Malaysia, exploring the indigenous concept of Molong and inviting users to form immersive relationships with nature."}]}, "developer_name": "Naqib Izzuddin Bin Hussien, Diana Azlyz, Tariq Zaman", "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://github.co